\begin{center}
\section*{Topic 5: Generators}
\end{center}

\subsection*{1. Yield Syntax}

A function that contains \texttt{yield} is a \emph{generator function}.
The \texttt{yield} is similar to \texttt{return},
but we can re-enter the function after using the value.
Generator functions return a generator object when called.
The \texttt{next} function extracts the next yielded value from the generator object.
If there are no more values to yield (i.e. the generator object is empty),
then \texttt{next} raises \texttt{StopIteration}.

